<header><p class="st-kicker">caliphate · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Toucouleur Empire</h1><p class="st-meta">1848 CE – 1893 CE · capital Segou</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The empire created by the jihad of Umar Tall, which conquered Segou and Massina and stretched across the western Sahel until the French conquest.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-hadj-umar-tall">Umar Tall</a>, a Tijani scholar from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/imamate-of-futa-toro">Futa Toro</a>, returned from the pilgrimage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> with great prestige and in 1849 set up a fortified base at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dinguiraye">Dinguiraye</a>, on the edge of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/imamate-of-futa-jallon">Futa Jallon</a>. In 1852 he launched a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jihad">jihad</a>, conquering the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kaarta">Kingdom of Kaarta</a> in 1854, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bamana-empire">Bamana Empire</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segou">Segou</a> in 1861 and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/massina-empire">Massina Empire</a> in 1862.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The empire was held together by Umar's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toucouleur">Toucouleur</a> followers from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senegal">Senegal</a> valley, the authority of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tijaniyya">Tijaniyya</a> order and garrisons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/musket">musketeers</a>. It had little central administration: provinces were run by Umar's sons, nephews and commanders from fortified towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segou">Segou</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nioro-du-sahel">Nioro</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bandiagara">Bandiagara</a>. Umar was killed in 1864 during a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulbe</a> uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massina">Massina</a>, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmadu-tall">Ahmadu Tall</a> ruled from Segou amid rebellion and rivalry with his brothers.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>From 1890 the French under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-archinard">Louis Archinard</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/segou">Segou</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nioro-du-sahel">Nioro</a> and finally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bandiagara">Bandiagara</a> in 1893. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmadu-tall">Ahmadu</a> fled east and died in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>, and the lands became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-sudan">French Sudan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/toucouleur-empire.jpg" alt="Toucouleur Empire" width="320" height="162"><figcaption>Image: T L Miles · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umars_jihad_state_map_general_c1864.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1848 CE – 1893 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>caliphate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Segou</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Umar Tall, Ahmadu Tall, Tijani Tall</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (Tijaniyya)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Pulaar, Bambara</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mali">Mali</a>, <a href="/countries/senegal">Senegal</a>, <a href="/countries/guinea">Guinea</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tukulor Empire, Toucouleur Caliphate, Umarian state</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1870&amp;focus=toucouleur-empire" aria-label="Toucouleur Empire on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4510 1677 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Toucouleur Empire lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4830 1933L4830 1933M4830 1933L4888 1900M4830 1933L5054 728M4830 1933L4781 1962"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4830 1933h0M4888 1900h0M5054 728h0M4781 1962h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4830 1933h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4830 1933h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Segou. <a href="/atlas?year=1870&amp;focus=toucouleur-empire">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
